---
description: Blank lines separate phases inside a function body
globs: src/**/*.{cpp,h}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Function body phases

Inside a function, put a blank line between distinct phases — not between
tightly related lines of the same phase.

Typical phases: locals/setup, search/loop, failure (`throw` / early exit),
mutation (`push_back` / `erase`), `return`.

- Do blank: after a lookup loop before `throw` or before inserting; after
  `reserve` before the fill loop; after `find_if` before the miss check;
  before a final `return` when the body had more than one phase.
- Do not blank: inside a short `for`/`if` that only matches and returns;
  between a guard `if` and its immediate `throw` when that is the whole
  phase; between every statement “for air”.
